{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/pulls/1781","id":5486071447,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU7KX288AAAABRv7Olw","html_url":"https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/pull/1781","diff_url":"https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/pull/1781.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/pull/1781.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1781","number":1781,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Reuse one scoped exchange across two independent descriptors","user":{"login":"wakairo","id":6393110,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzOTMxMTA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6393110?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo","html_url":"https://github.com/wakairo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wakairo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Reuse one scoped exchange across independent descriptors\n\nThe caller constructs two live descriptors of the same two-`u8`-field nominal type before guarded byte planning and pure mode selection. The active descriptor receives the selected mode through a lexical loan of its original field. The loan closes before the caller binds an independent standby recovery literal and passes the corresponding field of the second original to the same registered writer. After both loans close, the caller observes each target and its own sibling, copies each displaced value from its own result binding, and returns unit.\n\nBoth registered call replays and the complete entry seal support the private C17 plan. The first updated original is still live at the second call's entry and the standby starts with its own constructor package. C17 creates two separate automatic objects and emits one writer definition and two ordered scoped calls. The named displaced Copy and direct displaced tail writer forms both pass. The previously adopted single and same-original controls emit byte-identical C17.\n\n## First refusal and verification\n\nThe original main and separate #1777 pins both accepted CHECK for the three distinct-original sources and first refused at C17 with `V1-BACKEND-UNSUPPORTED`. The adopted baseline reproduced all eleven rows. The candidate retains the two-inline, crossed read, wrong displaced Copy and same-root-with-two-constructors C17 refusals, and the escaping reference CHECK refusal.\n\nThe low-load forms measured 4032 bytes, active `19 → 31` retaining tag `83` and standby `43 → 7` retaining tag `127`. The high-load form measured 4096 bytes and active `19 → 73` with identical standby results. Both old returns came from their respective original addresses. GCC Release and Clang ASan/LSan/UBSan each passed the eleven-row matrix and 62 targeted regressions. The three new forms contributed 24 strict native runs per compiler configuration plus six separate sanitized native executions. Physical OOM checked 1,656 CHECK allocation failures including 16 actual whole-entry seal failures and 2,493 named-C17 failures per destination state and configuration. Exact rollback, no-clobber, absence and retry passed.\n\nThe first observer's named-Copy ID comparison and the prototype's literal-`u8` emission refusal are preserved in the raw inventory, alongside the corrected observations and adopted-base measurements.\n\n| Fixed input | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| HEAD | `d121c79a0f3cb94da1d2d15aaf789cc16a6e94f0` |\n| Tree | `803e2b2efddbd136004ab84cac52e4d9932181f9` |\n| Sole parent and adopted base | `32b63e7bea3be5fd6fafb9f11f8ea0a7fd2376cc` |\n| Full-index binary diff | 13 paths, 46,443 bytes, SHA-256 `09f72977395e293ee2cdfc4abae98de86f260926deed9cf98e6a73de1766a29b` |\n\n[Frozen FIRST](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1778#issuecomment-7153740450) · [LOCAL READY](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1778#issuecomment-7154112799) · [C PUBLIC DRAFT GO](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1778#issuecomment-7154130069)\n\nRefs #1778\n\n## Per-test timeout amendment\n\nThe current Draft HEAD is `27ac5abfe6d8fdb5d6cb59c5a8d0ec75b07ba7a1`. The fixed-input table above records the original candidate. This fast-forward gives just `p1773_sequential_writer_rollback.unit` a 180-second CTest timeout. The allocation sweeps, rollback and no-clobber assertions, and retry checks all remain in the test.\n\nThe first natural ASan Light A timed out at 90.06 seconds on the original candidate. C's same-checkout diagnostic replay passed #240 in 53.19 seconds and the whole shard passed 688/688. Both amended local three-worker runs passed #240, in 69.52 and 67.91 seconds, and both adjacent rollback cases passed. [First CI result](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/actions/runs/45557517904/job/139013044656) · [Diagnostic replay](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/actions/runs/45557517904/job/139022994609) · [Timeout LOCAL READY and evidence](https://github.com/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/issues/1778#issuecomment-7155208322)\n","created_at":"2026-11-25T06:00:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T08:06:43Z","closed_at":"2026-11-25T08:06:41Z","merged_at":"2026-11-25T08:06:41Z","merge_commit_sha":"629994f527ded64d755923dcf9a3df2de08eacf5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/wakairo/NewLang_Compiler/pulls/1781/commits","review_commen